     "file": "hekr114",
     "pages": 10,
     "head": "14 A PRESENTATION OF DANCE AND CHOREOGRAPHY You are familiar with the Nāṭyaśhāstra and the Abhinaya Darpaṇam now. In ancient times, when they were written, dance was usually called nr ̥ tta and nr ̥ itya or nartana, whereas dance-drama was called nāṭya. Have you ever wondered how dance originated? If you refer to your Grade 6 Arts textbook (Theatre), you will recall an interesting story about the birth of the performing arts. Similarly, you will learn about the birth of dance from the Abhinaya Darpanam. Brahma Deva, derived from all four Vedas, is said to have created the Nāṭya Veda, often referred to as called the fifth Veda. Brahma Deva gave Nāṭya Veda to a Rishi, Bharata Muni, who studied and mastered all three aspects of nr ̥ tta, nr ̥ itya and nāṭya. ch14_DANCE.indd 152ch14_DANCE.indd 152 19-06-2025 16:37:3419-06-2025 16:37:34 Reprint 2026-27"
